---
/* 3D printer: a slicer preview under the visitor's scrubber. */
import Tag from '../Tag.astro';
import { printSpec } from '../../../data/garage';
interface Props { mode: 'panel' | 'list' }
const { mode } = Astro.props;
---
{mode === 'panel' ? (
  <>
    <p>A slicer preview. Drag the scrubber, or use the arrow keys, and the bracket stacks up on the bed; the yellow band and the traced outline mark the layer being printed.</p>
    <label class="g-lbl" for="print-layer">Layer</label>
    <input class="g-range" id="print-layer" type="range" min="0" max={printSpec.layers} step="1" value={printSpec.start} data-layer />
    <div class="g-readout" aria-live="polite" data-read></div>
    <p>Model: a small functional bracket, a base plate with two screw holes, an upright and two gussets. 90 by 56 mm, 54 mm tall.</p>
    <p class="g-note"><Tag />Placeholder model and settings. Kevin's real prints, G-code and slicer settings come later.</p>
  </>
) : (
  <>
    <p>A slicer preview: drag the scrubber and a small functional bracket builds up layer by layer, with the layer count and height shown.</p>
    <p><Tag />The bracket is a placeholder model; real prints, G-code and settings follow later.</p>
  </>
)}
